WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.940
- Talk with a lot of people
that you think are inspiring.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.670
We do that still a lot, we
go to meet people that we

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.229
think are doing such a great
job, or that we look up to.

00:00:11.229 --> 00:00:13.775
And then you get so
much energy out of that.

00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:16.765
And I think that can
help you get a long way.

00:00:16.765 --> 00:00:20.759
- I'm Emilie Tabor, one
of the founders of IMA,

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:22.156
Influencer Marketing Agency.

00:00:22.156 --> 00:00:25.256
- I'm Maddie, I'm also one
of the founders of IMA,

00:00:25.256 --> 00:00:27.353
Influencer Marketing Agency.

00:00:27.353 --> 00:00:30.202
What we do is, we create
influence for marketing strategies

00:00:30.202 --> 00:00:32.202
for all sorts of brands.

00:00:33.262 --> 00:00:37.044
So we create the strategy
but we also fully execute it.

00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:40.497
So from influencer matchmaking,
to setting up the strategy,

00:00:40.497 --> 00:00:44.580
to full execution and
measurement, and reporting.

00:00:45.614 --> 00:00:47.455
- We started working
together on a platform

00:00:47.455 --> 00:00:48.975
called fashionista.com.

00:00:48.975 --> 00:00:52.009
This was more of a Pinterest,
but then for fashion.

00:00:52.009 --> 00:00:54.469
Maddie was there, more
from the influencer side,

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:56.051
really building up the influencer network,

00:00:56.051 --> 00:00:58.949
and also the strategic
side of the platform.

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.769
And I was there more for the
commercial end of the platform,

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:04.919
really seeing how we can
make it into a business.

00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:07.197
- I think, because we're still very young,

00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:10.667
a lot of people in our
team are the same age.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.393
So sometimes it's hard...

00:01:12.393 --> 00:01:14.982
or it's a challenge to
be part of the team,

00:01:14.982 --> 00:01:18.074
but also be a leader, so to say.

00:01:18.074 --> 00:01:20.840
As a young entrepreneur,
to set up a company

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.436
and also be an example
for the rest of the team.

00:01:25.436 --> 00:01:26.800
- We launched in 2010,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.713
but then we changed our
name around about 2012,

00:01:30.713 --> 00:01:33.061
to Influencer Marketing Agency.

00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:36.932
And that's when a lot of
things changed for us.

00:01:36.932 --> 00:01:39.675
The market started changing,
as well they started

00:01:39.675 --> 00:01:42.644
to know influencer marketing,
and what it entailed.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:44.878
So we didn't have to explain it as much.

00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:45.934
It was starting to become part of the

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:48.593
natural marketing mix for a lot of brands.

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:51.797
And also, we built up
such a track record that,

00:01:51.797 --> 00:01:55.403
we could really prove the
effect of influencer marketing.

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:57.229
- Of course we want to keep on growing,

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:01.074
but we want to keep on
pioneering in this field.

00:02:01.074 --> 00:02:04.082
We want to stay, not
necessarily the biggest,

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:06.103
I think it's more about
the best and the quality

00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:09.012
of our work that we wanna be known of.

00:02:09.012 --> 00:02:10.277
And then next to that,

00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:13.610
we want to also see what we can do more.

